* c1e-strings.cos — exercises both C1e bracket-strings and byte-strings,
* both `[`/`]`-delimited (plan/07-demo-app-and-verification.md edge cases;
* see docs/vs-caos-editor-architecture.md's Strings note). Layer 1's
* tokenizer treats both uniformly; the semantic-tokens overlay is what
* disambiguates them once resolved (byte-string modifier vs. plain string).
* Load this fixture against the C1 variant (C1e bracket-strings and the
* legacy `R`-repeat animation suffix are not valid in CV+ variants — see
* fixtures/bitflag-heavy.cos's golden-path sibling, which had to switch to
* a literal 255 for DS).

* Byte-string: digit/R content, used for ANIM's poseList argument. No
* spaces allowed in C1/C2 variants (unlike CV+, which also allows the
* space-separated form).
anim [0123R]

* C1e bracket-string: legacy alternative to a quoted string literal, valid
* wherever a plain [string]-typed parameter is expected (e.g. DBGM's
* debug-message argument).
dbgm [Hello world]
